Updated Golden Config jobs to route each device through its highest-weighted `GoldenConfigSetting` and honor that Setting's per-feature `enable_*` flag. Devices skipped because the winning Setting has the feature disabled log an `E3038` warning naming the Setting and weight; jobs with no eligible devices log a single `E3039` warning per feature. All in-scope Settings' repositories are still synced (so read-only consumers stay current), but only enabled Settings' repos are committed and pushed.
Navigation menu items, Git datasource contents, the Config Overview list-view columns, and the device Configuration template extensions are no longer hidden by the app-level `enable_*` settings; they are always registered and feature availability is now resolved per-`GoldenConfigSetting` at job runtime. UI warnings about disabled jobs now reflect whether any Setting enables the feature.
Weight ties between overlapping `GoldenConfigSetting` records now resolve deterministically to the lower-sorted Setting name instead of an arbitrary database row, in both `get_for_device` and the device-to-settings map.
Saving a `GoldenConfigSetting` with `enable_intended` enabled while `sot_agg_query`, `jinja_repository`, `jinja_path_template`, `intended_repository`, or `intended_path_template` is unset is still allowed, but now surfaces a non-blocking warning banner (mirroring the existing disabled-Job warning) naming the missing fields, since the Intended job cannot generate configurations for the Setting's devices until they are populated.
Changed the GraphQL query requirement on a `GoldenConfigSetting` to follow that Setting's own `enable_sotagg` flag instead of the app-level setting.
Changed the Config Overview actions menu to always offer the SoT Aggregate Data and Postprocessing actions; each action reports when the device's winning Setting has the feature disabled.
Changed the `Deploy Config Plans` job and Job Button to skip, with an `E3038` warning, any plan whose device is no longer in scope of a Golden Config Setting.
Changed the `E3018` error to name the Golden Config Setting that is missing a required value, and extended the check to the repositories each job reads.
Changed the Golden Config Settings list to show a Dynamic Group member count and the `enable_*` flags by default; the description and repository columns remain available through the table configuration.
Changed intended configuration postprocessing to render without SoT aggregation data when the device's Golden Config Setting has no GraphQL query, instead of raising an error.
